3. What was the easiest part of the class for you? Explain why.
Probably just working in groups, but it was for me the most beneficial because I could ask my partner, mainly Liam, where his head was at with what we were learning and whether he understood or not.

4. What part of the class surprised or interested you the most? Explain why.
Not to beat a dead horse, but the group activities suprised me because I usually don't like working with other people but I genuinely enjoyed it.

5. Give one piece of advice to a student just beginning a quarter of STAT 331 that will help them be successful in learning.
Make sure to do the labs way ahead of when they are due and then just ask your peers questions and get comfortable with the people around you.
